  "question": {
    "text": "Two satellites <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> move round the earth in the same orbit. The mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is twice the mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. The quantity which is same for the two satellites will be",
    "image": null
  },
